# Standalone Ouroboros clone (own git repo + 256MB venv + real .env); the
# engine Helix uses is vendored at backend/engine/ouroboros/.
/Ouroboros/

# Session logs / working notes (internal process chatter, not product docs).
#
# Matched anywhere in the name rather than only as a prefix or a suffix. The
# narrower patterns below left real gaps: `2026-08-14-baton-1.txt` is neither
# `baton*.txt` nor `*-baton.txt`, and a transcript is exactly the file most
# likely to have a secret pasted into it — this one had a JWT signing key in
# it, one `git add -A` away from being published.
*baton*.txt
*dump*.txt

# --- Not part of the product -----------------------------------------------
# Everything below still lives in this working directory; it is simply not
# something a visitor to the repository has any use for. Untracked rather than
# deleted, because the coursework artefacts are still needed for submission.
#
# Every pattern is anchored with a leading `/` so it matches the repo root
# only. Unanchored, `demo_artifacts/` would also swallow the backend's test
# fixtures and `Helix.html` would swallow `frontend/helix.html`.

# University submission: the report, its LaTeX source, the pitch, the brief.
/*.docx
/*.pdf
/Helix-LaTeX/
/Helix-LaTeX.zip
/latex.zip
/main.aux
/main.lof
/main.log
/main.lot
/main.out
/main.tex
/main.toc

# Internal handoffs between the three of us.
/BATON-*.md
/baton-2.md
/read.txt
/continue.txt

